
  <sn><md>### Organic and Inorganic Pollutants 

In the Atmosphere, Hydrosphere and Geosphere

Pollutants can be broadly classified into `organic` and `inorganic` pollutants. They enter the three major environmental compartments—**atmosphere (air), hydrosphere (water), and geosphere (soil/land)**—through `natural processes and human activities`.


**Organic vs Inorganic Pollutants**

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
```text
Environmental Pollutants
│
├── Organic pollutants
│   │
│   ├── Carbon-based compounds
│   ├── Often derived from living materials or fossil fuels
│   ├── Many are persistent and toxic
│   └── Examples
│       ├── Pesticides
│       ├── PAHs
│       ├── VOCs
│       ├── Petroleum hydrocarbons
│       └── PCBs
```
:::

:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
```text
Inorganic pollutants
│
├── Metals, minerals, salts, gases and other non-carbon
│   compounds
├── Often persistent in the environment
└── Examples
    ├── Pb
    ├── Hg
    ├── Cd
    ├── SO₂
    ├── NOₓ
    ├── Nitrates
    └── Phosphates
```
:::
:::


