<sn><md>### Atmosphere

| Type          | Major pollutants                                                  | Major sources                                                           | Effects                                                             |
| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Organic**   | VOCs, hydrocarbons, benzene, toluene, formaldehyde, PAHs, dioxins | Vehicle exhaust, industries, fuel combustion, biomass burning, solvents | Smog, respiratory problems, carcinogenic effects, ozone formation   |
| **Inorganic** | SO₂, NOₓ, CO, CO₂, NH₃, H₂S, particulate matter, heavy metals     | Industries, vehicles, power plants, mining, combustion                  | Acid rain, climate change, respiratory diseases, reduced visibility |

**Examples:**

* Organic: **benzene (C₆H₆)**, methane (CH₄), polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs)
* Inorganic: **SO₂, NO₂, CO, CO₂, Pb, Hg, Cd**

</md></sn><sn><md>### Hydrosphere

The hydrosphere includes **rivers, lakes, groundwater, oceans and wetlands**.

| Type          | Major pollutants                                                                                       | Major sources                                         | Effects                                                                 |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Organic**   | Petroleum hydrocarbons, pesticides, phenols, detergents, solvents, PAHs, sewage-derived organic matter | Industrial discharge, agriculture, sewage, oil spills | Oxygen depletion, toxicity, bioaccumulation, death of aquatic organisms |
| **Inorganic** | Heavy metals, nitrates, phosphates, chlorides, acids, alkalis, cyanides                                | Mining, fertilizers, industries, sewage, urban runoff | Eutrophication, toxicity, groundwater contamination                     |

**Examples:**

* Organic: **oil, pesticides, phenol, detergents**
* Inorganic: **Pb, Hg, Cd, Cr, NO₃⁻, PO₄³⁻**

A major effect of excessive organic matter in water is increased **BOD (Biochemical Oxygen Demand)**. Microorganisms consume dissolved oxygen while decomposing organic matter, which can cause **fish kills**.

Excess nitrate and phosphate can cause **eutrophication**, producing excessive algal growth and subsequent oxygen depletion.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Geosphere

The geosphere includes **soil, rocks, sediments and terrestrial land**.

| Type          | Major pollutants                                                                | Major sources                                                            | Effects                                                                       |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Organic**   | Pesticides, herbicides, petroleum hydrocarbons, PAHs, PCBs, solvents            | Agriculture, petroleum spills, industrial waste, improper waste disposal | Soil toxicity, reduced microbial activity, bioaccumulation, reduced fertility |
| **Inorganic** | Heavy metals, salts, acids, alkalis, nitrates, phosphates, radioactive elements | Mining, industries, fertilizers, pesticides, waste disposal              | Soil degradation, toxicity, groundwater contamination, reduced plant growth   |

**Examples:**

* Organic: **DDT, glyphosate, petroleum hydrocarbons, PCBs**
* Inorganic: **Pb, Cd, Hg, As, Cr, excess nitrate and salts**
</md></sn>